# Known Fortio users and the owner of their compatibility gate.
#
# Columns: <repo> <workflow> <mode> <input> <blocking> <full>
#   repo      GitHub repository in owner/name form.
#   workflow  workflow file on the repository's default branch.
#   mode      direct = this workflow can test a Fortio candidate directly;
#             delegated = a downstream of libneo, whose gate owns the test.
#   input     workflow_dispatch input used by the gate, or '-' when the
#             downstream has no candidate-ref override.
#   blocking  whether a failed direct gate blocks the Fortio pull request.
#   full      reserved for a separately dispatched slow suite.
#
# Direct users are dispatched by .github/workflows/downstream-gate.yml.
# Delegated users remain in this registry so new consumers are visible and so
# their compatibility owner is explicit. Update this file when a dependency
# edge or its candidate-ref input changes.
itpplasma/libneo main.yml direct fortio_ref yes no
itpplasma/NEO-2 unit-tests.yml delegated libneo_ref no no
itpplasma/NEO-RT test.yml delegated libneo_ref no no
itpplasma/SIMPLE main.yml delegated libneo_ref no no
itpplasma/MEPHIT main.yml delegated libneo_ref no no
itpplasma/KAMEL ci.yml delegated libneo_ref no no
itpplasma/rabe test.yml delegated libneo_ref no no
